@startuml
'==== Title ====
title "As a User, I want to use a Web UI to create a private list of my publications, \n give it a name, set a genre and, eventually, share it." - SD

'==== basic style ====
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

' ==== Actor and participants ====
actor User
participant ":Client" as CLI
participant ":Server" as SER
database "DB" as DB

User -> CLI : Show me what I can do here
activate CLI
CLI -> SER : OPTIONS /my-lists {...}
activate SER
SER --> CLI : [POST], [GET], [PATCH], [DELETE]
deactivate SER
CLI --> User : These are your available resources
deactivate CLI

User -> CLI : Show me my lists of items
activate CLI
CLI -> SER : GET /my-lists {...}
activate SER
SER -> DB : select
DB --> SER : data
SER --> CLI : HTTP STATUS 200 {...}
deactivate SER
CLI --> User : display lists of items
deactivate CLI

User -> CLI : publicly share my list
activate CLI
CLI --> User : for how many days?
deactivate CLI

User -> CLI : days
activate CLI
CLI -> SER : PATCH /my-lists/{listId}/visibility {"durationDays": 7}
activate SER
SER -> DB : select
DB --> SER : data
SER --> CLI : HTTP STATUS 200 {...}
deactivate SER
CLI --> User: Success!

@enduml